#: src/app/[lang]/blog/mint-alternatives-developers/page.tsx:1969
msgid "For developers, the path forward is clear: prioritize data ownership, choose open source when possible, and be skeptical of services that seem too good to be true."
msgstr "For developers, the path forward is clear: prioritize data ownership, choose open source when possible, and be skeptical of services that seem too good to be true."

#: src/app/[lang]/blog/local-first-movement-developers/page.tsx:623
msgid "For indie developers and small teams, this changes the economics of software development. You can build sustainable software without venture capital to fund server infrastructure."
msgstr "For indie developers and small teams, this changes the economics of software development. You can build sustainable software without venture capital to fund server infrastructure."

#: src/app/[lang]/blog/cloud-budgeting-privacy-risks/page.tsx:1203
msgid "For IT professionals who understand these tradeoffs, offline-first architecture offers a path forward. Your financial data deserves the same security posture you would apply to production credentials or customer data."
msgstr "For IT professionals who understand these tradeoffs, offline-first architecture offers a path forward. Your financial data deserves the same security posture you would apply to production credentials or customer data."

#: src/app/[lang]/blog/budgie-offline-financial-data/page.tsx:938
msgid "For more details on our security architecture, visit our security section. To see the complete source code and verify everything we have described, check out our open-source section."
msgstr "For more details on our security architecture, visit our security section. To see the complete source code and verify everything we have described, check out our open-source section."

#: src/app/[lang]/blog/local-first-movement-developers/page.tsx:422
msgid "For most personal productivity and finance applications, this trade-off is favorable. Users would rather work now and sync later than be blocked waiting for network access."
msgstr "For most personal productivity and finance applications, this trade-off is favorable. Users would rather work now and sync later than be blocked waiting for network access."

#: src/app/[lang]/blog/local-first-movement-developers/page.tsx:119
msgid "For nearly two decades, cloud computing has dominated how we build software. Every startup pitch deck featured the same architecture: thin client, thick server, data in the cloud. But something interesting is happening. A growing movement of developers, researchers, and companies are questioning this orthodoxy and building software that works differently. They call it <0>local-first software</0>."
msgstr "For nearly two decades, cloud computing has dominated how we build software. Every startup pitch deck featured the same architecture: thin client, thick server, data in the cloud. But something interesting is happening. A growing movement of developers, researchers, and companies are questioning this orthodoxy and building software that works differently. They call it <0>local-first software</0>."

